"""Chapter 15 content for the RDODI build: sources, findings, taxonomy and section bodies.
The book's chapter (Google Sheets) was read on automatetheboringstuff.com on 2026-10-12 (an HTTP fetch of
https://automatetheboringstuff.com/3e/chapter15.html; the page returned 200 and its sha256,
76d2dc655b248a48921855f81131b8e4eee296340ed77ae0423cd48b11166d1b, equals the chapterDigest the book's own chapter ontology
records - automate_python_3e_ch15_v1_0_0.ttl in the Ontologies repository; the commit the course pins was not opened). The online
materials of the 3rd edition (the zip No Starch Press links from its book page) were downloaded, and the two scripts of the chapter's
project, auditBoringcoin.py and addBoringcoinTransaction.py, were run in them as they are shipped. The EZSheets page and release
files, the Google Sheets, Drive, OAuth, Cloud and Help pages, the Python 3.14 documentation, the three RFCs, the OWASP and MITRE
pages and the pages of the stories were opened on the same day. Every behaviour was executed under Python 3.14.6 (installed with
uv) on Ubuntu 24.04 (Linux) with ezsheets 2026.4.28, the newest release on 2026-10-12, google-api-python-client 2.201.0,
google-auth 2.61.0 and google-auth-oauthlib 1.5.0.
Not executed, and said so where it comes up: every request made with an OAuth token to Google's servers. No Google account, no
OAuth consent in a browser and no Google Cloud project were available, so nothing that Google answers was observed: not the
creation of a spreadsheet, the title Google gives an upload, the parsing of USER_ENTERED values, the unquoted sheet title in a range,
the quota errors, the content of an export, the 6 columns of the produce sheet after the upload, the Google Forms tool, the console
pages and the revoking of credentials. What was run instead is the real library with the real google-api-python-client, which
builds each request and reads each answer, and a stand-in at the HTTP layer (class G, in the third-party script and repeated in
the programs below) that was written for this study, keeps every cell as text and does not parse a value; so an output shows what
the library asks for and what it does with an answer, not what Google answers. The sign-in was played where it could be: the
authorization URL is built without a network, a local server plays the token endpoint, a tampered token file stands in for
hostile code. The public sheets (Boringcoin, Bean Count, Sweigart Books) were read as CSV exports, the first two byte-identical to
the exports committed on 2026-10-01 in ch15-page/fixtures. The chapter's other printed programs are recorded in
08-tooling/ch15-page/third_party_record_v1_0_0.json by sen0414_ch15_thirdparty_v1_0_0.py, which re-checks them. What the public
sites and the shipped scripts did on the day is in ch15-page/live_observations_v1_0_0.json, and what one ezsheets program printed
under each of the seven 3.14 releases, 3.13 and 3.12, and the same cell session under three releases of ezsheets, is in
ch15-page/interpreter_record_v1_0_0.json. A claim not in this file was not made."""
